From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:00:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: match SCS descriptors on their client address

An SCS descriptor can name a client behind a 4-address peer, but
cfg80211_scs_evaluate() matches it against every MSDU sent to the peer.
The descriptor of one host thus classifies the flows of every other
host behind the same peer.

Only match a descriptor with a client against an MSDU whose destination
address equals it. The client is not a classifier parameter and does
not count towards the granularity of a descriptor.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

--- a/net/wireless/scs.c
+++ b/net/wireless/scs.c
@@ -833,6 +833,22 @@ static bool scs_desc_match(const struct
 	return any;
 }
 
+/* The client is not a classifier parameter, so it does not add to the count */
+static bool scs_desc_client_match(const struct cfg80211_scs_desc *desc,
+				  const struct cfg80211_flow_info *info,
+				  bool *undecided)
+{
+	if (is_zero_ether_addr(desc->client))
+		return true;
+
+	if (!(info->present & FLOW_F(ETH_DA))) {
+		*undecided = true;
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	return ether_addr_equal(desc->client, info->key.da);
+}
+
 static u16 scs_desc_param_count(const struct cfg80211_scs_desc *desc)
 {
 	unsigned int i;
@@ -862,7 +878,8 @@ static u16 scs_desc_param_count(const st
  * @verdict: receives the result
  *
  * When several descriptors match, the one with the most classifier parameters
- * wins. An equal count keeps the first.
+ * wins. An equal count keeps the first. A descriptor with a client only
+ * matches an MSDU addressed to that client.
  */
 void cfg80211_scs_evaluate(struct cfg80211_scs_desc * const *desc, u8 n_desc,
 			   const struct cfg80211_flow_info *info,
@@ -877,7 +894,8 @@ void cfg80211_scs_evaluate(struct cfg802
 		bool undecided = false;
 		u16 count;
 
-		if (!scs_desc_match(desc[i], info, &undecided)) {
+		if (!scs_desc_client_match(desc[i], info, &undecided) ||
+		    !scs_desc_match(desc[i], info, &undecided)) {
 			/* A missing parameter only matters without a match */
 			verdict->undecided |= undecided;
 			continue;
